WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.440
Budget, monitoring, and what lasts after the grant.

2
00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:07.310
This is the video for module three of Proposal Writing.

3
00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:16.120
The budget is your proposal written in numbers. Too high looks wasteful. Too low suggests you do not understand the work.

4
00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:27.160
Each line shows the item, the unit, the quantity and the unit cost. For example, 2 trainers, for 12 days, at 25,000 naira per day.

5
00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:38.280
The total is quantity times unit cost: 600,000 naira. Group your lines into categories, and always use the funder's template if it gives one.

6
00:00:39.530 --> 00:00:48.030
For example, Amaka prices every line from 2 or 3 market quotes in Lafia. The course figures are illustrative and approximate.

7
00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:55.140
Personnel, a part-time coordinator and two trainers: 1,200,000 naira.

8
00:00:56.390 --> 00:01:02.940
Materials, including 40 starter kits and safety gear: 1,320,000 naira.

9
00:01:04.190 --> 00:01:09.290
Venue, transport and refreshments: 1,440,000 naira.

10
00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:17.640
Business support, 290,000 naira, and monitoring and evaluation, 250,000 naira.

11
00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:35.900
Direct costs come to 4,500,000 naira. Administration at 7%, within the call's cap, adds 315,000 naira. Her request is 4,815,000 naira, under the 5,000,000 maximum.

12
00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:39.810
Direct costs are spent only on this project.

13
00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:48.700
Indirect costs are your shared running costs. Many funders allow them only up to a stated percentage. Never exceed it.

14
00:01:49.950 --> 00:02:02.410
In-kind contributions are things you provide yourself. Amaka's cooperative gives a storage room worth 180,000 naira. Show it in a separate column, because it proves commitment.

15
00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:06.490
And leave ineligible costs, like vehicles, out completely.

16
00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:19.970
Budget notes explain each line in one to three sentences. For example: 1,000 naira per woman per training day covers a return fare. Without it, the poorest members could not attend.

17
00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:26.270
Check that every activity has a cost line, and every cost line links to an activity.

18
00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:29.040
Keep your quotes on file.

19
00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:34.400
Leave out ineligible costs, and keep administration within the cap.

20
00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:44.040
Use a spreadsheet so totals calculate automatically, then check that the summary, narrative and cover letter all show the same figures.

21
00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:59.730
Monitoring tracks activities and outputs while the project runs. Evaluation judges whether outcomes were achieved. Every indicator needs a baseline, a target, a data source, a timing and a responsible person.

22
00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:09.050
At the end of month 4, Amaka's sales records show 22 of 40 women selling at least twice a month. Her target is 30.

23
00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:16.650
She looks for a pattern. Most of the women not selling live far from the market and have no regular buyers.

24
00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:27.180
So she pairs women to sell together at the weekly market, and introduces 3 school bursars to the group. By month 5, 27 sell regularly.

25
00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:37.310
By month 6, 31 of 40 sell regularly, above target. Her report states the low figure, the reason, the change and the result.

26
00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:48.690
Sustainability means explaining which benefits last after the money ends, and how. The state government will take over is weak, unless you have a letter saying so.

27
00:03:49.940 --> 00:04:03.740
Amaka gives concrete mechanisms. The cooperative will charge members 5,000 naira per place for a second training, as agreed at its general meeting. 6 of the strongest women become peer trainers.

28
00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:14.030
Each woman saves 500 naira from every 5,000 naira of sales to buy her next batch, and links with 3 schools create regular buyers.

29
00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:22.300
Claiming no risks looks naive. List what could go wrong, how likely and how serious it is, and your response.

30
00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:35.330
Because her training uses caustic soda, Amaka plans for chemical burns: safety gear for every woman, a lye safety demonstration first, and a first aid kit and clean water at every session.

31
00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:43.780
She also buys materials in bulk in month 1, and agrees the schedule with participants to avoid busy farming and festive weeks.

32
00:04:45.030 --> 00:04:57.410
Your practice. Build your budget in a spreadsheet, with real quotes and notes for your biggest lines. Draft your M&E plan table. Write at least three sustainability mechanisms and a risk table.

33
00:04:57.760 --> 00:05:03.000
Then score your draft against the funder's criteria. Now continue with the lessons below.
